{
  "$comment": "GENERATED by `npm run grammar` from packages/driftscript/src/compiler/tokens.ts. Never hand-edit: the next generation discards it without saying so. `npm run grammar:check` fails when this file is stale.",
  "name": "DriftScript",
  "scopeName": "source.driftscript",
  "fileTypes": [
    "drs"
  ],
  "patterns": [
    {
      "include": "#comment"
    },
    {
      "include": "#string"
    },
    {
      "include": "#annotation"
    },
    {
      "include": "#number"
    },
    {
      "include": "#keyword"
    },
    {
      "include": "#type"
    },
    {
      "include": "#declaration"
    },
    {
      "include": "#operator"
    }
  ],
  "repository": {
    "comment": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "name": "comment.line.double-slash.driftscript",
          "match": "//.*$"
        },
        {
          "name": "comment.block.driftscript",
          "begin": "/\\*",
          "end": "\\*/"
        }
      ]
    },
    "string": {
      "name": "string.quoted.double.driftscript",
      "begin": "\"",
      "end": "\"",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "name": "constant.character.escape.driftscript",
          "match": "\\\\."
        }
      ]
    },
    "declaration": {
      "$comment": "A name in a declaring position, so `data Door` highlights `Door` as a type rather than as a variable. The keyword itself is matched by the generated keyword rule; this only names what follows it. Order is load-bearing twice over: TextMate takes the first match, so a rule with a clause must precede the plain form it extends — `data Wolf : Dog` before `data`, and `component Transform from host` before `component`. The entity-form rules are appended rather than interleaved because no earlier rule can match their heads, and `scripts/grammar.test.mjs` reads the first three by position.",
      "patterns": [
        {
          "$comment": "`data Wolf : Dog` — the base is a type too. Without this the record reads as declared and its base as an ordinary word, which is the one part of the line a reader is looking for.",
          "match": "\\b(data)\\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\\s*(:)\\s*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)",
          "captures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "keyword.declaration.driftscript"
            },
            "2": {
              "name": "entity.name.type.driftscript"
            },
            "3": {
              "name": "keyword.operator.driftscript"
            },
            "4": {
              "name": "entity.name.type.driftscript"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "match": "\\b(data|enum)\\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)",
          "captures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "keyword.declaration.driftscript"
            },
            "2": {
              "name": "entity.name.type.driftscript"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "match": "\\b(fn|task|state)\\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)",
          "captures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "keyword.declaration.driftscript"
            },
            "2": {
              "name": "entity.name.function.driftscript"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "$comment": "`component Transform from host` — the assertion direction. It must precede the plain `component` rule, because TextMate takes the first match and the plain rule would consume the head and leave `from host` unhighlighted, which is the one part of that line that says the declaration creates nothing.",
          "match": "\\b(component)\\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\\s+(from)\\s+(host)",
          "captures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "keyword.declaration.driftscript"
            },
            "2": {
              "name": "entity.name.type.driftscript"
            },
            "3": {
              "name": "keyword.declaration.driftscript"
            },
            "4": {
              "name": "keyword.declaration.driftscript"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "match": "\\b(component|entity|prefab)\\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)",
          "captures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "keyword.declaration.driftscript"
            },
            "2": {
              "name": "entity.name.type.driftscript"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "$comment": "A system is named like a function rather than like a type: it is a body that runs, and the schedule addresses it by that name.",
          "match": "\\b(system)\\s+([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)",
          "captures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "keyword.declaration.driftscript"
            },
            "2": {
              "name": "entity.name.function.driftscript"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "keyword": {
      "name": "keyword.control.driftscript",
      "match": "\\b(component|continue|require|become|import|return|entity|system|prefab|writes|update|await|spawn|state|enter|event|match|while|break|scope|reads|after|query|false|task|data|enum|from|else|emit|true|let|var|for|mut|fn|if|in|on|as|at)\\b"
    },
    "type": {
      "name": "support.type.primitive.driftscript",
      "match": "\\b(String|Entity|bool|i16|i32|i64|u16|u32|u64|f32|f64|i8|u8)\\b"
    },
    "annotation": {
      "name": "entity.name.function.decorator.driftscript",
      "match": "@(deterministic|replicated|aiContext|substance|reaction|aiTool|editor|pure|hot)\\b"
    },
    "number": {
      "patterns": [
        {
          "match": "\\b([0-9]+(?:\\.[0-9]+)?)(degC|kPa|mol|deg|rad|ms|Hz|kJ|MJ|kg|Pa|J|K|W|g|m|s)\\b",
          "captures": {
            "1": {
              "name": "constant.numeric.driftscript"
            },
            "2": {
              "name": "constant.numeric.unit.driftscript"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "constant.numeric.driftscript",
          "match": "\\b[0-9]+(?:\\.[0-9]+)?\\b"
        }
      ]
    },
    "operator": {
      "name": "keyword.operator.driftscript",
      "match": "(\\|\\||&&|\\+%|\\+\\||-%|-\\||\\*%|\\*\\||\\+=|-=|\\*=|\\/=|==|!=|<=|>=|=>|\\?\\.|\\.\\.|->|\\{|\\}|\\(|\\)|\\[|\\]|,|:|;|\\.|\\?|\\+|-|\\*|\\/|%|=|<|>|!|\\||&)"
    }
  }
}
